-- title:
--   Complex powers through the operator logarithm
-- statement:
--   For an operator $A$ on a nonzero finite-dimensional complex Hilbert space, define the totalized complex-power expression
--   $$
--   A^{[z]}=\exp(z\log A),\qquad z\in\mathbb C,
--   $$
--   using continuous functional calculus for the operator logarithm and the normed-algebra exponential. On faithful positive operators this is the usual complex power and supports the holomorphic interpolation family. On the kernel of a singular positive operator, $\log0=0$ makes this exponential power act as the identity, unlike the support-zero convention for nonzero real CFC powers. Positivity and faithfulness are explicit premises of results identifying it with real functional-calculus powers; the raw definition itself is totalized for every operator.
-- source:
